---
export const prerender = true;
import "../styles/global.css";
import LandingLayout from "@kaiplan/marketing/layouts/landing-layout.astro";
import { publicSiteCopy } from "@kaiplan/knowledge/marketing";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
import { buildAppSignupUrl } from "@/lib/app-links";

const openAppUrl = buildAppSignupUrl();
---

<LandingLayout
  config={siteConfig}
  description="Kaiplan is a solo, bootstrapped wedding planning workspace. One builder, one product, paid for by couples. Learn who builds it and why."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  title="About - Kaiplan"
>
  <article class="editorial-shell" data-page="about">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="about-hero-headline">
      <div class="hero__grid">
        <div class="hero__primary">
          <p class="editorial-eyebrow">About</p>
          <h1
            id="about-hero-headline"
            class="editorial-display-l hero__headline"
          >
            One product. One builder. Paid for by couples.
          </h1>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__lede-band">
          <p class="editorial-lede hero__lede">
            Kaiplan is a bootstrapped wedding planning workspace. There is no PE
            firm, no venture round, no thousand-person product org behind it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="editorial-rule chapter-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

    <!-- CHAPTER I -->
    <section
      class="chapter chapter--narrow"
      aria-labelledby="about-solo-heading"
    >
      <p class="editorial-eyebrow">I. The operation</p>
      <h2 id="about-solo-heading" class="editorial-display-m chapter__title">
        A solo, bootstrapped operation.
      </h2>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        Kaiplan is built and maintained by one person. Not a startup with a
        runway and a growth team, not a PE-backed rollup adding tools to a
        marketplace. One engineer, one product, funded by the couples who use
        it. That is not a caveat. It is the point.
      </p>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        Most wedding tools are free because vendors pay for the placements you
        see inside them. That model means the platform earns from the vendors,
        not the couples, which means every recommendation is shaped by who is
        paying. Kaiplan earns from couples directly. The pricing is on the page.
        The features are the product. There is no ad inventory to sell.
      </p>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        I read every customer complaint personally. Every support email, every
        bug report, every piece of feedback lands in my inbox and I respond to
        it. That is not a PR commitment — it is just how a one-person product
        works. You are not writing into a ticket queue; you are writing to the
        person who will fix it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="editorial-rule chapter-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

    <!-- CHAPTER II -->
    <section
      class="chapter chapter--narrow"
      aria-labelledby="about-bugs-heading"
    >
      <p class="editorial-eyebrow">II. Bug fixes</p>
      <h2 id="about-bugs-heading" class="editorial-display-m chapter__title">
        A 24-hour bug-fix promise.
      </h2>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        If you find a bug that breaks your workflow — something that stops you
        from saving a guest, updating a budget line, or generating a seating
        assignment — write to <a
          class="editorial-link"
          href="mailto:angel.campa@kaiplan.app">angel.campa@kaiplan.app</a
        >. I commit to a fix within 24 hours for anything that blocks core
        planning work. Not a workaround, not a timeline — a fix.
      </p>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        Kaiplan is a paid product. If it does not work, you should not be paying
        for it. The 24-hour window reflects that. Non-blocking improvements and
        feature work move at a different cadence, but broken core features do
        not wait.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="editorial-rule chapter-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

    <!-- CHAPTER III -->
    <section
      class="chapter chapter--narrow"
      aria-labelledby="about-contact-heading"
    >
      <p class="editorial-eyebrow">III. How to reach me</p>
      <h2 id="about-contact-heading" class="editorial-display-m chapter__title">
        Email and LinkedIn.
      </h2>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        For support, feedback, or anything about the product: <a
          class="editorial-link"
          href="mailto:angel.campa@kaiplan.app">angel.campa@kaiplan.app</a
        >. I respond personally and I keep every conversation in context — if
        you wrote last month, I remember it.
      </p>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        If you want to see what else I am building or follow the product
        publicly: <a
          class="editorial-link"
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/angelcampa1/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">linkedin.com/in/angelcampa1</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="editorial-rule chapter-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

    <!-- CLOSING CTA -->
    <section
      class="chapter chapter--narrow chapter--close"
      aria-labelledby="about-close-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="about-close-heading" class="editorial-display-m chapter__title">
        {publicSiteCopy.pricingTrialBannerText}
      </h2>
      <p class="editorial-body chapter__body">
        Budget, guest list, seating, and vendor tracking in one workspace.
        <a class="editorial-link" href={openAppUrl}>Start planning</a> and keep the
        spreadsheets as a backup if you want — most couples stop needing them after
        the first week.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</LandingLayout>

<style>
  [data-page="about"] {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .hero__primary {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .hero__lede-band {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero__lede {
    max-width: 38ch;
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
      align-items: end;
      gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    }
    .hero__lede-band {
      text-align: right;
      align-items: flex-end;
    }
    .hero__lede {
      text-align: right;
      max-width: 32ch;
    }
  }

  .chapter-rule {
    margin-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 0;
  }

  .chapter {
    padding-block-end: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .chapter--narrow {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .chapter--close {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .chapter__title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .chapter__body {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .chapter__body + .chapter__body {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
